  "raw_text": "139\n\nLiura\n \n–\n \nin the water\n \n/ en el agua\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb54\n):\n \nJona win “P\nâ\nsa tara\n \ntakaskbia dukiara, liura ai lulks”\n \n–\n \nJona said: “In order for the strong wind to stop, throw\n\nme in the water”\n \n/ Jon\nás\n \ndijo: \"Para que el fuerte viento se detenga, tírame al agua\"\n)\n\nLî Pangkaia\n \n(Alt:\n \nPangkaia\n) (\ndict,dictu,my,lv,bh\n;\n \nPanhkaia\n-lfb,dictu-alt;\n \nPankaia\n-incorrect spelling /ortografía\nincorrecta) (v)\n \n–\n \nto draw water, to pick up water\n \n/ sacar agua, recoger agua\n\nLibait L\nȃ\nka\n \n(\ndb,dba\n;\n \nLevítico\n-dbta\n;\n \nLivait Lâka\n-bw\n)\n \n–\n \nLeviticus\n \n(Bible book) / Levítico (libro bíblico)\n\nLih\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsea turtle\n \n/ tortuga marina\n\nLih Mairin kati\n \n–\n \nMay\n \n/ mayo\n\n(Lit:\n \nfemale sea turtle moon\n \n/ luna de tortuga marina hembra\n)\n\nLih Wainhka kati\n \n–\n \nApril\n \n/ abril\n\n(Lit:\n \nmale sea turtle moon\n \n/ luna de tortuga marina ma\ncho\n)\n\nLih\n \nwîn\na\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nturtle meat\n \n/ carne de tortuga\n\nLihkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nWlihkaia\n;\n \nLaik kaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto like, to love, to delight in\n \n/ gustar, amar, deleitarse\n\nLalihkra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nperson who likes, person who loves\n \n/ persona que le gusta, persona que ama\n\nLihngni\n \n(\ndict\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nable to hear\n \n/ capaz de escuchar\n\nKiama lihngni\n \n(\ndict\n;\n \nKiama lihni\n-\ndb,dictu-alt\n;\n \nKiama lingni\n-\ndictu\n;\n \nKyama lihni\n-\nlv\n)\n \n–\n \nattentive, obedient, submissive\n\n/ atento, obediente, sumiso\n\nLihni\n \n(\ndict\nu,dict\n)\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nnaked\n \n/ desnudo\n\nKiama lihni\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nKiama\n \nlihngni\n\nLika\n \n–\n \nis, are,\n \nam,\n \nis\n/are/am\n \ninstead,\n \ninstead,\n \nwhereas\n, in contrast, is\n/are/am\n \nin contrast\n, on the contrary, (he/she/it) is/\n\n(we/they/you) are/ (I) am on the contrary\n \n/ es, son,\n \nsoy, somos, eres, sos,\n \nes\n/son/soy/somos/eres/sos\n \nen cambio, en\n\ncambio, mientras que, en contraste,\n \nestoy/\nestá\ns/está,estamos/\nestán en contraste\n,\n \nal contrario, al contrario\n\nes/son/soy/somos/eres/sos\n\n(Note/Nota: Most often, this word is in the middle of a phrase or sentence and not usually at the end like is most often the case\nwith other verbs.\n \nSimilar words are:\n \nSika\n \nand\n \nMika\n.\n \n/ La mayoría de las veces, esta palabra está en el medio de una frase u\n\noración y no generalmente al final, como suele ser el caso con otros verbos. Palabras similares son:\n \nSika\n \ny\n \nMika\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n02/20\n):\n \nAna rayaka ra d\nî\na chens takan, kuna d\nî\na\n \nlika chens takras kan ki?\n \n–\n \nIn Hannah’s life, what changed but what\n\non the contrary\n \nwas not changed?\n \n/ En la vida de Ana, ¿qué cambió pero\n \npor el contrario,\n \nqué no cambió?\n)\n\nKaka lika\n \n–\n \nonly if, if instead\n \n/ solo si, si en cambio\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb\n-\n32\n):\n \nBarac D\né\nbora ra win: “Wamna, yang wal wama kaka lika”\n \n–\n \nBarak said to Deborah: ”I will go, but only if\n\nyou go with me”\n \n/\n \nBarac le dijo a D\né\nbora: “Voy, pero solo si t\nú\n \nvas conmigo”\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh\n-\n142\n):\n \nAisa\n-\nyapti\n \nmita diara kum G\nâ\nd l\nâ\nka mapara makabisa kaka lika,\n \nluhpia ba b\nî\nla walras kaia sip sa\n \n–\n \nOnly if\n\nparents ask something against God’s law, (then) the child is able not to obey\n \n/\n \nSolo si los padres piden algo en contra de la\n\nley de Dios, (entonces) el ni\nñ\no puede no obedecer\n)\n\nLila\n \n(1) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nconcubine, mistress, lover\n \n/ concubina, amante, querido\n,\n \nquerida\n\nLila\n \n(2) (n/s,adj)\n \n–\n \nmiddle, center\n \n/ medio, centro\n\nLila kat bapi buaia\n \n(\nvi,wqu-5/22\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto remain neutral\n \n/ mantenerse neutral\n\nLila kat kaia\n \n(\nt14\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto be neutral\n \n/ ser neutral\n\nLila mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto place in the middle\n \n/ colocar en el medio\n\nLilak\n \n(a/t:\n \nLila bâk\n)\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nthrough the middle, through the center\n \n/ por el medio, por el centro\n\nLilara\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nin the middle, in the center\n \n/ en el medio, en el centro\n\nLila\npas\n \n–\n \nmiddle, center\n \n/ medio, centro\n\nLilapasra\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nLila pasra\n-\nmy45\n)\n \n–\n \nin the middle, in the cent\ner\n \n/ en el medio, en el centro\n\nLilia\n \n(adj\n,\nadv\n)\n \n–\n \njoy\nful, happy\n \n/ alegre, feliz\n\nBan lilia kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto continue to be\n \nhappy\n \n/ seguir siendo feliz\n\nGâd lilia pali ba\n \n(\ntnm\n-\n1Tim 1:11\n)\n \n–\n \nthe happy God\n \n/ el Dios feliz\n\nKau lilia\n \n–\n \nmore joyful, happier\n \n/ más alegre, más feliz\n\nLilam\n \n–\n \nyour joy, your happiness, your boyfriend, your girlfriend, your love\n \n/ tu alegría, tu felicidad, tu novio, tu\nnovia, tu amor\n\nLili\n \n–\n \nmy joy, my happiness, my boyfriend, my girlfriend, my love\n \n/ mi alegría, mi felicidad, mi novio, mi novia, mi\namor\n\nLilia bîla yabaia\n \n(\ntkl\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto give commendation\n \n/ dar encomio\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nBîla pain (nani) wiaia\n)",
